# AI Answer Latency and Quality Qualification Procedure

Status: DONE
Milestone: A0 Procedure definition only
Dependencies: None
Execution status: NOT_STARTED

## Purpose

Compare actual transcription-to-answer configurations without replacing quality or privacy with a fast-looking token.

## Inputs

Implemented stage instrumentation and fake-stream tests; approved synthetic corpus/rubrics;
authorized deployment/account/budget if cloud calls will run; exact model/API/SDK/runtime/source identity.

## Procedure

1. Run local draft/source/commit/stream state and failure tests before any cloud call.
2. Replay identical synthetic PCM without speakers/microphone; record capture/ASR/commit/draft stages.
3. Obtain the actual approved model/version/deployment/processing policy and a bounded spend cap.
4. Run one fixed baseline with standard filtering and one active Ask; separate cold and warm samples.
5. Compare candidate configurations with randomized/interleaved order and equal useful-answer constraints.
6. Measure Ask-to-first-rendered-text, first-useful-sentence, completion/cancel/error rates and quality.
7. Record tokens, actual tier/caching, retry outcomes and cost; never drop failed/incomplete samples silently.
8. Tune one bottleneck at a time: capture/commit, output length/reasoning, model, API or eligible tier.
9. Qualify the exact candidate UI/capture/privacy behavior and obtain owner usability approval.
10. Publish a bounded result table and preserve rejected candidates/uncertainty.

## Stop conditions

Unapproved cloud data/budget, source contamination, lost question tail/negation, unreliable cancellation,
silent retry/egress, content-logging leakage, wrong answer used as a speed win, or unsupported lifecycle/model.

## Tasks

- [x] Define staged local-first evaluation and explicit cloud authorization boundary.
- [x] Require comparable quality, visible latency and reproducible identities.
- [x] State that research/targets are not measured Azure results.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Procedure separates batch RTF, ASR finalization, API TTFT and user-visible useful-answer latency.
- [x] A model is called fastest only within a named, measured, quality-qualified comparison.

